{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>This shall be My holy anointing oil.</b> Ramban, of blessed memory, explained: it should have said 'it shall be for Aaron and his sons,' yet it says 'this shall be for Me' — to anoint with it My holy anointed one whom I choose, for all your generations — so that you not understand the verse which says 'and whoever puts any of it on a stranger (זר) shall be cut off' to mean that זר is anyone who is not of the seed of Aaron the priest; for if so, how were the kings of Israel, who were not priests, anointed with the anointing oil? Therefore this verse comes — 'this shall be for Me' — to include the kings within the category of the priesthood, for both are anointed of HaShem. And this is what it says concerning David (1 Samuel 16:12): ״קום משחהו כי זה הוא״ — 'Arise, anoint him, for this is he.' And Scripture also says (Psalms 89): ״מצאתי דוד עבדי בשמן קדשי משחתיו״ — 'I have found David My servant; with My holy oil I have anointed him' — that is, with the oil that is 'anointing of holiness to Me.' And therefore it says here: 'upon the flesh of a man (אדם) it shall not be poured' — and אדם is to be understood in the sense of an ordinary person, not a king. And you must grasp that the reason Scripture placed the passage of the oil first and the passage of the incense last is because they correspond to the head and the end. For with the oil they anointed him in the shape of a כ\"ף, and it is the supreme among all liquids, and from it indeed comes the 'anointing of holiness,' in the manner of ״שאו ידיכם קדש״ — and this is the language of 'anointing oil of holiness,' and it is written: ״ויעש את שמן המשחה קדש״. And the incense is for the final ה of the Name, for concerning it is written (Deuteronomy 33:10): ״ישימו קטורה באפך״. And for this reason there were five kinds in the anointing oil, corresponding to the five initial letters, and in the incense nine kinds, for thus it comprises all of them and comes the passage of the incense in the language of ויאמר — and understand this." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> 'Anointing oil of holiness, this shall be for Me' — Rabbi Yehudah bar Rabbi Elai taught: the anointing oil that Moses made in the wilderness — miracles upon miracles were performed in it from beginning to end. For at the beginning it contained only twelve log, as it says: 'and oil of olive, a hin.' If you were to smear with it the roots alone, it would not suffice for even one — how much the more so, since the fire consumes, and the cauldron boils, and the spices absorb! And from it were anointed the Tabernacle and all its vessels, and all the vessels of the altar, and the laver and its base; and from it Aaron and his sons were anointed during the seven days of consecration; and from it the High Priests were anointed; and all of it endured for the time to come, as it says: 'anointing oil of holiness, this shall be for Me.' ז\"ה in gematria is twelve log, and so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded. There are eleven spices: eleven spices were stated to Moses at Sinai — סמים, תרי, נטף, ושחלת, וחלבנה — these are five; to include again the like of these — that makes ten; and לבונה זכה — that makes eleven."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:56.496601094Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}